              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "11004189"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Phosphatase catalytic subunit of the trehalose synthase complex that catalyzes the production of trehalose from glucose-6-phosphate and UDP-alpha-D-glucose in a two step process (PubMed:11004189). The disaccharide trehalose serves as a storage carbohydrate that is mobilized during nutrient stress and spore germination (Probable). Together with ntp1, regulates the level of trehalose as a protectant for cell integrity during thermal, osmotic, and oxidative stress (Probable)"
        }
      ],
